WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:05.510
- Everybody in my family catches lobster.

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:08.280
Me and my sister are
fourth-generation lobstermen.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.750
Throughout these generations
of all of us lobstering,

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.920
the lessons I've learned
about sustainability are,

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.710
if we don't protect it now,
then we're not gonna have

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:18.660
it in the future.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.210
I'm Heather Thompson. I am Captain

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:28.320
of fishing vessel Gold Digger.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.680
With my sister Hillary as my sternman.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:35.550
My great-grandfather was a lobsterman,

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:39.630
my grandfather was a lobsterman,
my dad is a lobsterman,

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:42.390
my two sons are lobstermen, and my niece

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:43.930
is a lobstermen.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:45.460
My name is Laney, and I'm a fifth

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:47.130
generation lobster fisherman.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.360
- [Heather] It's what we all do.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:53.600
It's really, it's a
physically demanding job.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.820
I mean, you have to worry about the tides,

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:01.490
bait, getting your
rope, buoys, your traps,

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:04.230
so many things, it's even hard to fathom

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.270
until you actually have to go and do it.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.160
One of the sayings my father
used to say was “Be somebody.”

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:13.110
You know, it doesn't matter
if, if we were a guy

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:16.000
or a girl on the back, it's
like, if you wanna do it,

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:16.833
you can do it.

00:01:16.833 --> 00:01:18.000
You just have to make sure

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.420
you push yourself. Be somebody.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:21.650
Do it.

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:23.710
He's taught me just
about everything I know,

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:25.710
especially the
sustainability of lobster,

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:28.520
making sure that we're
protecting our own future.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.800
and my children's
generation to catch lobster.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.720
We plan to do this the rest of our lives,

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:35.880
if it allows us.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:40.900
- Lobster fishermen have
been practicing sustainable

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.610
fishing for many generations,

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:45.190
before the regulations
even came into effect.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:48.960
- We inspect every single
lobster we pull aboard.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:51.770
If it's undersized, we throw it back,

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:55.040
and if it's oversized, we throw it back.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:58.970
- [Skip] We want the
resource to be sustainable,

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:03.010
and if we take the big
ones and harvest them,

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:06.050
then there's not lobster
for future generations.

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:08.420
- [Heather] When we pull
up a lobster that has eggs

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:11.570
on it, we take our tool,
and we make a little nick

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:13.760
in its tail, we call it V-notch;

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:15.860
it makes a little V in the fin.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:17.050
- [Skip] That means you throw it back

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:18.970
because it's an egg-bearing female.

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:21.460
And that's important for
the future sustainability

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.520
of the lobster population.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.370
- Our future is worth more than that.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.750
- [Skip] We're really
appreciative of the job

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:31.930
the fishermen do day in and day out.

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:34.510
It's a tough job, and we
establish face-to-face

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:37.550
meetings with them so we can
understand their business,

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:39.530
who their family is, and
what their challenges

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:40.870
and opportunities are.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:45.430
It helps us to keep the resource
vibrant for future years.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:47.030
And it helps them meet our needs

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:49.270
and get the highest quality seafood.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:52.350
- If we don't take care of our future,

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:54.350
then nobody else will.

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:55.780
It's our kid's future.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:59.690
- My grandfather always
told me to be somebody.

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:01.560
It means to, like, work hard

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.890
and do your best at whatever you do.

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:05.840
And the name of my boat is Be Somebody.

00:03:07.771 --> 00:03:11.490
- For these 50 years,
throughout these generations

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:14.710
of all of us lobstering, my
great-grandfather practiced

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:18.560
sustainability of lobsters.
He protected the lobsters

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:21.710
he threw back to ensure that my generation

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:24.650
and my children's generation would be able

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:26.190
to catch lobster.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.690
When a lobster is put on somebody's plate

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:31.650
and brought to them, and they look at it,

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:35.200
I want them to think of
how much of a tradition,

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.370
and how much time and effort and thought

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:41.000
went into this catch.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.900
It's a lot of generations,
a lot of learning,

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.960
a lot of hard work, a lot of
time, that went into that.

